---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="HowNote — Engineering Tools, Pipe Sizes & Standards Intelligence"
  description="Calculate, convert and review practical pipe-size and standards information, then turn known requirements into a Purchase Note draft."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Find · Compare · Calculate · Decide</div>
    <h1>Practical engineering tools for real purchasing decisions.</h1>
    <p>HowNote begins with fast calculators and size references, then connects them to standards evidence, compatibility analysis and supplier-facing sourcing checks.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/tools/pipe-weight-calculator">Calculate pipe weight</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/tools/dn-nps-a-converter">Convert DN / NPS / A</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/howspec/purchase-note">Build a Purchase Note draft</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container grid">
    <article class="card featured-card">
      <div class="eyebrow">HowNote Tools</div>
      <h2>Calculate and convert</h2>
      <p class="muted">Pipe weight, nominal-size cross-reference, mm–inch, kg–lb and MPa–psi tools run directly in the browser.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/tools">Browse tools →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Size Reference</div>
      <h2>Keep nominal and actual separate</h2>
      <p class="muted">DN, NPS and regional A labels are shown separately from actual OD, wall thickness and calculated ID.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/sizes">Browse sizes →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Standards Evidence</div>
      <h2>See the source type</h2>
      <p class="muted">Official metadata, manufacturer references, regional aliases and calculated outputs are not presented as the same evidence.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/standards">Browse standards →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card featured-card">
      <div class="eyebrow">HowSpec</div>
      <h2>Turn open questions into a supplier draft</h2>
      <p class="muted">The first Purchase Note Builder separates standards, actual size, material, inspection, documents, marking, packing and unresolved confirmations.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/howspec">Explore HowSpec →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container related-section">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">HowNote workflow</div>
      <h2>From an input value to a purchase check.</h2>
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <div><strong>1. Calculate</strong><span>Weight, quantity and unit results</span></div>
        <div><strong>2. Convert</strong><span>DN, NPS, A and engineering units</span></div>
        <div><strong>3. Verify</strong><span>Standard identity, edition and source</span></div>
        <div><strong>4. Compare</strong><span>Dimensions, materials and test requirements</span></div>
        <div><strong>5. Decide</strong><span>Compatibility and purchase-note checks</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">Calculator, converter, standards evidence and a preliminary Purchase Note Builder are live. Standard Compare and Compatibility remain planned until verified data can support them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
